Kenfing-Rousseau; the Elements of the History of England by Milot (to injure, if possible, a translation of the same work by Mrs Brooke); and produced several dramatic performances, together with an infinite variety of publications both original and translated. To him also the public are indebted for the collection (imperfect as it is) of The Poetical Works of Robert Lloyd, M.A., 1774, 2 vols 8vo. Dr Kenrick died June 9, 1777.
